{"url": "https://www.sdstate.edu/programs/graduate/plant-science-phd", "final_url": "https://www.sdstate.edu/programs/graduate/plant-science-phd", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-29", "text": "Plant Science (Ph.D.) | Academic Program | South Dakota State University\nSkip to main content\nApply\nVisit\nDirectories\nDegree Finder\nFaculty and Staff\nOffice Directory\nBuildings Directory\nEvent Calendar\nCampus Map\nSDSTATE\nSearch\nVisit\nDegree Finder\nCampus Map\nSDSTATE\nSearch\nFilter by Topic\nBlog Event News Profile Program\nClose Search Box\nMain Navigation\nAbout\nAbout Us\nUniversity Facts\nNews\nSandbox Login\nAwards and Rankings\nConsumer Information\nAccreditation\nAcademics\nColleges and Departments/Schools\nGeneral Education\nAcademic Calendar\nAcademic Catalog\nGraduate School\nHonors College\nLibrary\nAdmissions\nUndergraduate\nTransfer\nGraduate\nInternational Undergraduate\nOnline\nDual Credit\nPaying for College\nStudent Life\nHousing\nCampus Dining\nStudent Success\nStudent Experience\nUniversity Wellbeing\nParents and Families\nResearch\nEvents and Trainings\nFind Funding\nResearch Impact\nProposal Development\nResearch Support\nStudent Research Opportunities\nCommunity\nAttractions\nCamps and Conferences\nFamily Weekend\nSDState Experience\nSDSU Metro Center\nEvent Calendar\nSearch\nApply Today\nSDSTATE\nBreadcrumb\n...\nHome\nAcademics\nDegree Finder\nPlant Science (Ph.D.)\nPlant Science (Ph.D.)\nPh.D.\nBrookings Main Campus\nRapid City\nShare\nTwitter\nLinkedin\nFacebook\nEmail\nPrint\nApply Now\nMore Information\nTransforming Global Agriculture.\nThe Department of Agronomy, Horticulture and Plant Science is a nationally recognized educational and research institute.\nOur graduate students conduct original research and are trained in investigative techniques by experienced faculty. Graduate training also includes classroom instruction, teaching experience and meaningful experiences in laboratory, greenhouse and field research techniques.\nThe department encourages collaborations among disciplines and research programs that support graduate training. Students can pursue their graduate studies within the integrated research programs of:\nArboriculture\nCrop science\nEntomology\nGenomics and genetics\nPlant biotechnology\nPlant breeding\nPlant pathology\nPrecision agriculture\nSeed technologies\nSoil science and biogeochemistry\nViticulture\nWater management\nWeed science\nOur faculty members will guide Ph.D. students to tailor academic and research programs to fit their career goals and personal preferences. Our recent graduates are employed as postdoctoral researchers or lecturers at universities or U.S. Department of Agriculture-Agricultural Research Service research centers and as scientists in the agriculture industry.\nVisit Department\nView Requirements\nCost and Aid\nQuick Facts\nLocations\nBrookings Main Campus, Rapid City\nCredits\n60 Credit Plan\n90 Credit Plan\nEst. Time to Completion\n3-5 years\nStart Term\nFall, Spring, Summer\nIs it for you?\nThis program will be a good fit if you:\nHold an undergraduate degree in agriculture, biology, botany, horticulture, agriculture, environmental science, natural resources or other related fields.\nHave a strong interest in advancing the field of plant science.\nWant to lead research in the lab and out in the field.\nCan think critically and creatively about complex problems.\nJob Outlook\nBack to top\nCareer Opportunities\nExplore possible career opportunities with this degree:\nAgricultural consultant (domestic or international)\nAgricultural chemical researcher or sales manager\nCommercial crop or greenhouse manager\nFood processing scientist\nPlant biotechnologist\nPlant breeder\nPlant industry or biofuels researcher\nPlant-pest protection specialist\nSenior scientist or program leader for a federal or state agriculture, environmental quality or land management agency\nUniversity professor, research support scientist or extension educator\nReady to take the next step?\nContact Our Department\nKaren Sanguinet\nVisit Department\n605-688-5123\nHelpful Resources\nProgram Requirements\nDomestic Applicants\nInternational Applicants\nTuition and Funding\nGraduate Assistantships\nApply Now\nGraduate Admissions\nGraduate School\nYou may also be interested in...\nBiological Sciences (Ph.D.) \u2013 Natural Resource Management Specialization\nGraduate\nBiological Sciences (Ph.D.) \u2013 Plant Molecular Biology Specialization\nGraduate\nBiological Sciences (Ph.D.) \u2013 Food Science Specialization\nGraduate\nBiochemistry (Ph.D.)\nGraduate\nChemistry (Ph.D.)\nGraduate\nBiological Sciences (Ph.D.) \u2013 Plant Science Specialization\nGraduate\nBiological Sciences (Ph.D.) \u2013 Agricultural and Biosystems Engineering Specialization\nGraduate\nVisit Us\nCome Meet Your Future\nMeet the people that will help shape your future and define your college experience! Learn more about your academic interests with some of our world-class faculty.\nApply Today\nPlan Your Visit\nRequest Info\nGet Directions\nGive to SDSU\nOffice Directory\nExplore\nAbout SDState\nAcademics\nAdmissions\nStudent Life\nResearch\nCommunity\nConnect\nAlumni\nAthletics\nBookstore\nEvent Calendar\nGiving\nLibrary\nNews\nFor Students\nD2L\nJacks Club Hub\nJacks Email\nMyJacks Card\nMyState\nSelf Service\nFor Faculty and Staff\nEmployment\nFaculty and Staff Directory\nInsideState\nMy Account\n\u00a9 2026 All Rights Reserved.\nEmergency\nEAO\nLegal\nMission\nPolicies\nReport It\nSDState Facebook\nSDState X.com\nSDState Youtube\nSDState Instagram\nSDState LinkedIn\nSearch\nFilter by Topic\nBlog Event News Profile Program\nAbout\nAbout Us\nUniversity Facts\nNews\nSandbox Login\nAwards and Rankings\nConsumer Information\nAccreditation\nAcademics\nColleges and Departments/Schools\nGeneral Education\nAcademic Calendar\nAcademic Catalog\nGraduate School\nHonors College\nLibrary\nAdmissions\nUndergraduate\nTransfer\nGraduate\nInternational Undergraduat